namespace pdg { /**

\var object pdg::NetClient::connection

\brief reference to the NetConnection, or boolean false if not yet connected

The property starts as the literal \c false. After the underlying socket connects,
it holds a NetConnection. It is not a general boolean flag, and assigning a
connection does not by itself mean the PDG protocol handshake has completed.
Use the connect callback to know when the connection is ready for application
messages.

\note A retained connection object is not proof that its socket is still open.
Use the connection callbacks to track disconnection and errors.

\see NetClient::connect(), NetConnection

**/ }
